[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A .sgra file cannot carry a generated-file header, because it has no comment syntax

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SGRA-ADMITS-NO-COMMENTS
TITLE: A .sgra file cannot carry a generated-file header, because it has no comment syntax
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The grammar for .sgra files admits nothing before [GRAMMAR] and nothing between
its keys. A leading # line fails the textx parse at 1:1 with
Expected '[GRAMMAR]', and there is no alternative comment production anywhere in
the file. Measured against strictdoc 0.28.3.

Every other generated artefact in this repository opens with a line saying it is
generated and naming its generator. A .sgra emitted by the grammar surface
cannot, so docs/sdoc/grammar.sgra will look hand-written forever and a session
editing it by hand gets no warning at the point of editing. The only places a
banner could hide are a field HUMAN_TITLE or an element PREFIX, both of which
change what the file means.

Whatever marks the file as generated therefore has to live outside it -- a
sibling README, a treefmt or check rule that regenerates and diffs, or a path
convention. Undecided which.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Noted while building the negative fixture corpus, where the same limitation
forced the per-fixture expectation out of the fixture files and into their
README.
<<<
